      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1844, Bluffton sparked the Bluffton Movement, a protest against federal taxes that foreshadowed South Carolina’s secession.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluffton%2C_South_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Bluffton Oyster Company, family‑owned and riverfront, is a landmark where locals enjoy fresh seafood and river views.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoversouthcarolina.com/bluffton",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1998 Heyward House opened to the public, preserving a 19th‑century home as part of Bluffton Historical Preservation Society.",
